  <p>In gaming, your name is everything. It's what teammates call you in voice chat, what opponents see on the kill feed, and what shows up on leaderboards. A generic name blends into the background. A name with <strong>small text</strong> — superscript numbers, small caps clan tags, bold characters — gets noticed, remembered, and sometimes even feared.</p>

  <p>But not every game handles Unicode the same way. Some accept almost anything (Minecraft Java Edition), others have strict character filters (Roblox), and a few (like League of Legends) fall somewhere in between. This guide covers the compatibility of every major game with all 9 small text styles, plus nickname ideas that won't get you reported.</p>

  <h2>Game-by-Game Compatibility</h2>

  <h3>Valorant</h3>
  <p><strong>Compatibility: Excellent.</strong> Riot's tactical shooter has the best Unicode support of any competitive game. Superscript letters, superscript numbers, and small caps all render cleanly in your name and in-game chat.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Name examples:</strong> "Phantom⁰⁷", "ᴀᴄᴇᴜ" (ACEU in small caps)</li>
    <li><strong>Agent select screen:</strong> Names display in full — your styled name shows up exactly as entered</li>
    <li><strong>Kill feed:</strong> Unicode characters appear correctly in the kill feed, making your name stand out even there</li>
    <li><strong>Best styles:</strong> Superscript letters + superscript numbers, Small Caps, Bold</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Fortnite</h3>
  <p><strong>Compatibility: Good, but with caveats.</strong> Epic Games supports Unicode in display names, but periodically updates its name filtering policy. Superscript and Small Caps have historically worked well.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Name examples:</strong> "Tilted²⁰²⁶", "ɢʜᴏsᴛ" (GHOST in small caps)</li>
    <li><strong>Warning:</strong> If your name stops displaying after an update, Epic may have tightened character restrictions. Superscript numbers are the most future-proof choice</li>
    <li><strong>Best styles:</strong> Superscript numbers, Small Caps</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Steam</h3>
  <p><strong>Compatibility: Partial.</strong> Steam profile names support most Unicode, but the in-game overlay strips certain characters depending on the game. What works on your profile may not work in CS2 or Dota 2.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Name examples:</strong> "ᴘʀᴏᴅɪɢʏ", "Carry¹"</li>
    <li><strong>Profile vs In-game:</strong> Small Caps and Bold render beautifully on Steam profiles; in-game behavior depends entirely on the game's character filter, not Steam's</li>
    <li><strong>Best styles:</strong> Small Caps, Bold, Superscript numbers</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>League of Legends</h3>
  <p><strong>Compatibility: Limited.</strong> Riot's name filter is stricter than Valorant's. Superscript numbers usually pass, but superscript letters are frequently blocked. Small Caps is hit-or-miss depending on the patch.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Name examples:</strong> "Mid²⁰²⁶", "Jungle⁰⁷"</li>
    <li><strong>Safe approach:</strong> Regular letters + superscript numbers at the end. Don't try full superscript names — Riot's filter will reject them</li>
    <li><strong>Best styles:</strong> Superscript numbers only</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Minecraft (Java Edition)</h3>
  <p><strong>Compatibility: Excellent.</strong> Java Edition has near-complete Unicode support. Every style in our generator works, including Bubble Text, Bold, Italic, and Bold Italic. This is the most small-text-friendly game on the list.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Name examples:</strong> "ⓈⓉⒺⓋⒺ", "𝐇𝐞𝐫𝐨𝐛𝐫𝐢𝐧𝐞"</li>
    <li><strong>Server compatibility:</strong> Some servers restrict Unicode characters in chat, even if they appear in your name. Check server rules</li>
    <li><strong>Bedrock Edition:</strong> More restrictive than Java. Stick to superscript and numbers on Bedrock</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Roblox</h3>
  <p><strong>Compatibility: Limited.</strong> Roblox has aggressive character filtering. Most styled Unicode characters are rejected in usernames and display names.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>What works:</strong> Basic superscript numbers (¹²³) sometimes pass. Anything else is likely blocked</li>
    <li><strong>Best styles:</strong> Superscript numbers ¹²³ only, and even those aren't guaranteed</li>
  </ul>

